01:12:38,500 --> 01:12:45,820
Not at all. I would argue that the others, the other teachers were detached because they didn't see that potential in their students.

581
01:12:47,000 --> 01:12:53,600
Marva Collins was very much connected and she focused on the positive and created the benefits.

582
01:12:55,360 --> 01:13:01,600
Abraham Maslow, not only does love perceive potentialities, but it also actualizes them.

583
01:13:02,820 --> 01:13:10,320
Let me tell you a quick story about Tommy.

584
01:13:10,740 --> 01:13:16,460
And as I mentioned to you, Tommy is the consummate merit finder. In fact, she's a merit creator.

585
01:13:17,140 --> 01:13:22,320
So this was at a time when Tommy was eight months pregnant.

586
01:13:24,600 --> 01:13:25,560
Huge baby.

587
01:13:26,280 --> 01:13:28,560
Those of you who know David, he's a very big baby.

588
01:13:28,940 --> 01:13:30,460
You know, like father, like son.

589
01:13:31,860 --> 01:13:33,940
So this is eight months pregnant.

590
01:13:35,580 --> 01:13:42,600
And Tammy takes me for one of those talks that those of you in long-term relationships know about.

591
01:13:43,080 --> 01:13:47,460
And she says, Tal, you know, this is getting really heavy.

592
01:13:47,820 --> 01:13:56,160
This is really difficult for me, and I just need your help more. You just need to help me a little bit more in the house.

593
01:13:58,110 --> 01:14:07,710
And I said to her, fine. I felt so sheepish and so inconsiderate. I said, no, I'm sorry, fine. So what can I do?

594
01:14:07,790 --> 01:14:19,310
And she said, you know, shopping this afternoon would help. I just can't carry these bags anymore. So I went over to Star Market, filled up the entire refrigerator, not only brought the things home, but actually put them in the refrigerator.

595
01:14:21,230 --> 01:14:23,590
And because, you know, I felt so guilty.

596
01:14:24,350 --> 01:14:35,590
And then Tommy saw that and she said, you know, thank you so much for doing it. And I said to Tammy, Tammy, you know, I'm really sorry that you had to tell me.

597
01:14:35,770 --> 01:14:43,570
I should have done it without you. And she said, no, no, no, no. You know, this is what I love about you so much. You're so considerate and you listen to me when I talk.

598
01:14:44,050 --> 01:14:45,370
So I did the dishes too.

599
01:14:48,640 --> 01:14:55,480
Again, benefit creating rather than only benefit finding or focusing on what doesn't work.

600
01:14:56,680 --> 01:15:06,400
I will not see you on Tuesday. I'm away for almost for the whole week of Passover, but you're going to have a treat on Tuesday with an amazing lecture by Sean on humor. I'll see you.
